---
functor: 1
title: From LaTeX
---

set heading(numbering: none)

Functor is not compatible with LaTeX, and it does not try to be. This page maps LaTeX to Functor so that people and AI models can move a document by hand or with a converter. Where Functor has a meaning form, use it. For example, write `object vec: v` once, not `v.arrow` in each place.

# Rules that change most

| LaTeX habit | Functor |
|:--|:--|
| `\name` | `name`, with no backslash |
| `{...}` for a group | `(...)` for a group |
| `ab` for a times b | `a b`, with a space |
| `\command{x}` for an accent or a font | `x.operation` |
| `&` and `\\` in align | one step on each line in display math |
| `\text{...}` | `"..."` |
| `\newcommand` | `sym name = recipe` |

# Accents and fonts

| LaTeX | Functor | Result |
|:--|:--|:-:|
| `\hat{\theta}` | `theta.hat` | $theta.hat$ |
| `\tilde{x}` | `x.tilde` | $x.tilde$ |
| `\bar{x}`, `\overline{x}` | `x.bar` | $x.bar$ |
| `\dot{x}`, `\ddot{x}` | `x.dot`, `x.ddot` | $x.dot + x.ddot$ |
| `\check{f}`, `\breve{u}` | `f.check`, `u.breve` | $f.check + u.breve$ |
| `\vec{v}` | `v.arrow`, or `object vec: v` | $v.arrow$ |
| `\underline{x}` | `x.under` | $x.under$ |
| `\mathbf{A}`, `\boldsymbol{\alpha}` | `A.bold`, `alpha.bold` | $A.bold + alpha.bold$ |
| `\mathbb{R}` | `R.bb` | $R.bb$ |
| `\mathfrak{g}` | `g.frak` | $g.frak$ |
| `\mathcal{L}` | `L.cal` | $L.cal$ |
| `\mathscr{L}` | `L.script` | $L.script$ |
| `\varphi`, `\epsilon`, `\vartheta` | `phi.alt`, `epsilon.alt`, `theta.alt` (the other form of `phi`, `epsilon`, `theta`) | $phi.alt + epsilon.alt + theta.alt$ |
| `\varphi` in the whole file | `set greek(phi: alt)`, then plain `phi` | $phi.alt$ |
| `\mathring{x}`, `\overrightharpoon{x}` | `x.ring`, `x.harpoon` | $x.ring + x.harpoon$ |
| `\mathbb{1}`, `\Bbbk` | `1.bb`, `k.bb` | $k.bb$ |
| `\upmu` | `mu.up` | $mu.up$ |
| `\mathrm{d}x` | `d.up x` | $d.up x$ |
| `\boxed{x}` | `(x).box` | $(x).box$ |

# Relations and operators

| LaTeX | Functor | Result |
|:--|:--|:-:|
| `\neq`, `\leq`, `\geq` | `eq.not`, `le`, `ge` | $eq.not, le, ge$ |
| `\in`, `\notin`, `\ni` | `in`, `in.not`, `ni` | $in, in.not, ni$ |
| `\subset`, `\subseteq`, `\not\subset` | `subset`, `subseteq`, `subset.not` | $subset, subseteq, subset.not$ |
| `\approx`, `\sim`, `\equiv`, `\propto` | `approx`, `sim`, `equiv`, `propto` | $approx, sim, equiv, propto$ |
| `\to`, `\gets`, `\mapsto` | `to`, `gets`, `mapsto` | $to, gets, mapsto$ |
| `\Rightarrow`, `\Leftarrow`, `\Leftrightarrow` | `implies`, `implies.flip`, `iff` | $implies, implies.flip, iff$ |
| `\times`, `\cdot`, `\pm`, `\div` | `times`, `cdot`, `pm`, `div` | $times, cdot, pm, div$ |
| `\cup`, `\cap`, `\setminus` | `cup`, `cap`, `setminus` | $cup, cap, setminus$ |
| `\oplus`, `\otimes`, `\odot` | `plus.circle`, `times.circle`, `cdot.circle` | $plus.circle, times.circle, cdot.circle$ |
| `\boxplus`, `\boxtimes` | `plus.box`, `times.box` | $plus.box, times.box$ |
| `\forall`, `\exists`, `\nexists` | `forall`, `exists`, `exists.not` | $forall, exists, exists.not$ |
| `\partial`, `\nabla`, `\infty` | `partial`, `nabla`, `infty` | $partial, nabla, infty$ |
| `\hbar`, `\ell`, `\aleph` | `h.cross`, `ell`, `aleph` | $h.cross, ell, aleph$ |
| `\ldots`, `\cdots` | `dots`, `cdots` | $dots, cdots$ |
| `\emptyset` | `emptyset` | $emptyset$ |
| `\ll`, `\gg`, `\lll` | `lt.x2`, `gt.x2`, `lt.x3` | $lt.x2, gt.x2, lt.x3$ |
| `\prec`, `\succ`, `\preceq` | `prec`, `succ`, `stack(prec, eq)` | $prec, succ, stack(prec, eq)$ |
| `\leqslant`, `\lesssim`, `\lessgtr` | `le.alt`, `stack(lt, sim)`, `stack(lt, gt)` | $le.alt, stack(lt, sim), stack(lt, gt)$ |
| `\cong`, `\simeq`, `\asymp`, `\doteq` | `cong`, `simeq`, `asymp`, `eq.dot` | $cong, simeq, asymp, eq.dot$ |
| `\sqsubset`, `\sqsubseteq` | `subset.square`, `subseteq.square` | $subset.square, subseteq.square$ |
| `\subsetneq`, `\Subset` | `stack(subset, eq.not)`, `subset.x2` | $stack(subset, eq.not), subset.x2$ |
| `\vdash`, `\dashv`, `\models`, `\Vdash` | `proves`, `proves.flip`, `models`, `forces` | $proves, proves.flip, models, forces$ |
| `\top`, `\bot`, `\neg` | `bot.flipv`, `bot`, `lnot` | $bot.flipv, bot, lnot$ |
| `\therefore`, `\because`, `\Diamond` | `therefore`, `because`, `diamond` | $therefore, because, diamond$ |
| `\multimap`, `\parr` | `lollipop`, `par` | $lollipop, par$ |
| `\ltimes`, `\rtimes`, `\wr` | `ltimes`, `rtimes`, `wr` | $ltimes, rtimes, wr$ |
| `\sqcup`, `\sqcap`, `\uplus`, `\amalg` | `sqcup`, `sqcap`, `uplus`, `coprod` | $sqcup, sqcap, uplus$ |
| `\oslash`, `\circledast`, `\circledcirc` | `div.circle`, `ast.circle`, `circ.circle` | $div.circle, ast.circle, circ.circle$ |
| `\dotplus`, `\bullet`, `\dagger`, `\ddagger` | `plus.dot`, `bullet`, `dagger`, `ddagger` | $plus.dot, bullet, dagger, ddagger$ |
| `\triangleleft` (normal subgroup), `\bowtie`, `\pitchfork` | `normal`, `bowtie`, `pitchfork` | $normal, bowtie, pitchfork$ |
| `\perp\!\!\!\perp` (independent) | `indep` | $indep$ |
| `\leftrightarrow`, `\uparrow`, `\downarrow` | `tofro`, `to.rot`, `to.flip.rot` | $tofro, to.rot, to.flip.rot$ |
| `\Uparrow`, `\Downarrow`, `\updownarrow` | `implies.rot`, `implies.flip.rot`, `tofro.rot` | $implies.rot, implies.flip.rot, tofro.rot$ |
| `\longrightarrow`, `\Longrightarrow`, `\longmapsto` | `to.wide`, `implies.wide`, `mapsto.wide` | $to.wide, implies.wide, mapsto.wide$ |
| `\hookrightarrow`, `\rightarrowtail`, `\twoheadrightarrow` | `incl`, `mono`, `epi` | $incl, mono, epi$ |
| `\yo` (Yoneda embedding) | `yo` | $yo(A)$ |
| `\rightleftharpoons`, `\rightharpoonup` | `equil`, `to.harpoon` | $equil, to.harpoon$ |
| `\rightrightarrows`, `\rightleftarrows` | `stack(to, to)`, `stack(to, to.flip)` | $stack(to, to), stack(to, to.flip)$ |
| `\nrightarrow`, `\nRightarrow` | `to.not`, `implies.not` | $to.not, implies.not$ |
| `\vdots`, `\ddots`, `\iddots` | `vdots`, `ddots`, `udots` | $vdots, ddots, udots$ |
| `\complement`, `\wp`, `\beth` | `complement`, `wp`, `beth` | $complement, wp, beth$ |
| `\imath`, `\jmath`, `\digamma` | `imath`, `jmath`, `digamma` | $imath, jmath, digamma$ |
| `\prime`, `\dprime`, `\trprime` | `prime`, `prime.x2`, `prime.x3` | $prime, prime.x2, prime.x3$ |
| `^\circ`, `\permil`, `\qed` | `degree`, `permille`, `qed` | $degree, permille, qed$ |
| `\Finv`, `\Game`, `\mho` | `F.turn`, `G.turn`, `Omega.turn` | $F.turn, G.turn, Omega.turn$ |
| `\flat`, `\natural`, `\sharp`, `\clubsuit`, `\bigstar`, `\checkmark` | `flat`, `natural`, `sharp`, `clubs`, `blackstar`, `checkmark` | $flat, natural, sharp, clubs, blackstar, checkmark$ |

# Large operators

| LaTeX | Functor | Result |
|:--|:--|:-:|
| `\sum_{k=1}^{n}` | `sum_(k = 1)^n` | $sum_(k = 1)^n$ |
| `\prod`, `\coprod` | `prod`, `coprod` | $prod, coprod$ |
| `\int_0^1 f\,dx` | `integral_0^1 f dd x` | $integral_0^1 f dd x$ |
| `\sum_{\substack{p \text{ prime} \\ p \le n}}` | `sum_(p "prime"; p le n)` | $sum_(p "prime"; p le n)$ |
| `\smashoperator`, `\mathclap` | not needed: a wide limit goes under clear neighbours | $x = sum_(1 le i lt j le n) a_i b_j$ |
| `\iint`, `\iiint`, `\oint` | `integral.x2`, `integral.x3`, `integral.circle` | $integral.x2, integral.x3, integral.circle$ |
| `\bigcup`, `\bigcap` | `union`, `inter` | $union, inter$ |
| `\bigwedge`, `\bigvee` | `wedge.big`, `vee.big` | $wedge.big, vee.big$ |
| `\bigoplus`, `\bigotimes`, `\bigodot` | `plus.circle.big`, `times.circle.big`, `cdot.circle.big` | $plus.circle.big, times.circle.big, cdot.circle.big$ |
| `\biguplus`, `\bigsqcup` | `uplus.big`, `sqcup.big` | $uplus.big, sqcup.big$ |
| `\iiiint`, `\fint` | `integral.x4`, `integral.cross` | $integral.x4, integral.cross$ |
| `\limsup`, `\liminf`, `\operatorname*{arg\,max}` | `limsup`, `liminf`, `argmax` | $limsup_(n to infty) a_n$ |
| `\operatorname{Hom}`, `\operatorname{rank}` | `Hom`, `rank` | $Hom(A, B)$ |
| `\lim_{n\to\infty}` | `lim_(n to infty)` | $lim_(n to infty)$ |

# Fractions, roots, brackets

| LaTeX | Functor | Result |
|:--|:--|:-:|
| `\frac{a}{b}` | `frac(a, b)` | $frac(a, b)$ |
| `\sqrt{x}` | `sqrt(x)` | $sqrt(x)$ |
| `\binom{n}{k}` | `binom(n, k)` | $binom(n, k)$ |
| `\left( \frac{a}{b} \right)` | `(frac(a, b))` | $(frac(a, b))$ |
| `\left[ 0, \frac{1}{2} \right)` | `[0, frac(1, 2))` | $[0, frac(1, 2))$ |
| `\lvert x \rvert`, `\lVert v \rVert` | `abs(x)`, `norm(v)` | $abs(x) + norm(v)$ |
| `\langle u, v \rangle` | `inner(u, v)` | $inner(u, v)$ |
| `\lfloor x \rfloor`, `\lceil x \rceil` | `floor(x)`, `ceil(x)` | $floor(x) + ceil(x)$ |
| `\llbracket x \rrbracket` | `(x).brack.x2` | $(x).brack.x2$ |

The n-th root, `\sqrt[n]{x}`, has no form yet.

# Environments

| LaTeX | Functor |
|:--|:--|
| `\begin{pmatrix} a & b \\ c & d \end{pmatrix}` | `mat(a, b; c, d)` |
| `bmatrix`, `vmatrix`, `Bmatrix` | `mat(...)` with `set mat(fence: brack)`, `vbar` or `brace` |
| `smallmatrix` | `mat(...)` in running text; it is small by default |
| `\xrightarrow{f}`, `\xleftarrow[g]{}` | `to^f`, `gets_g` |
| `\overset{\text{def}}{=}`, `\stackrel{?}{=}` | `=^"def"`, `=^"?"` |
| tikz-cd: `A \arrow[r, "f"] \arrow[d, "g"'] & B \\ C` | `diagram(...)`: see [Diagrams](structures/diagrams.html) |
| tikz-cd: `\arrow[r, bend left]`, `bend right` | `A to.bend B`, `A to.bend.flipv B` in a `diagram` |
| tikz-cd: `\arrow[Rightarrow, from=1, to=2]` (a 2-cell) | `alpha: f implies g` in a `diagram` |
| tikz-cd: `crossing over` | automatic: the arrow written first gets a gap |
| `\begin{cases} x & x \ge 0 \\ -x & x < 0 \end{cases}` | `cases(x, x ge 0; -x, x lt 0)` |
| `\begin{align} a &= b \\ &= c \end{align}` | `$$`, then `a = b`, then `  = c` on the next line |
| `\begin{theorem}[Name] \label{thm:a}` | `::: theorem {#thm:a title="Name"}` |
| `\begin{proof} ... \end{proof}` | `::: proof` ... `:::` |
| `\begin{figure} ... \caption{...}` | `::: figure` with a line `Caption: ...` |
| `\begin{itemize} \item` | `- item` |
| `\begin{enumerate} \item` | `1. item` |
| `\begin{verbatim}` | three backticks |

# Document

| LaTeX | Functor |
|:--|:--|
| `\documentclass`, `\usepackage` | nothing. Use `set` rules. |
| `\title{}`, `\author{}`, `\date{}` | front matter: `title:`, `author:`, `date:` |
| `\section{Intro}\label{sec:intro}` | `# Intro {#sec:intro}` |
| `\subsection{}` | `## ...` |
| `\emph{x}`, `\textbf{x}` | `*x*`, `**x**` |
| `\ref{thm:a}`, `\eqref{eq:a}` | `@thm:a`, `@eq:a` |
| `\cite{knuth84}` | `[@knuth84]` |
| `\footnote{text}`, `\marginpar{text}` | `^[text]` |
| `\href{url}{text}` | `[text](url)` |
| `\includegraphics{plot}` | `![alt](plot.svg)` |
| Two backticks and two apostrophes for quotes; `--`, `---`, `~` | `"quotes"`, `--`, `---`, `~` |
| `\newcommand{\R}{\mathbb{R}}` | `sym RR = R.bb` |

# Spaces

| LaTeX | Functor |
|:--|:--|
| `\,`, `\:`, `\;` | `thin`, `med`, `thick` |
| `\quad`, `\qquad` | `quad`, `qquad` |
| `\!` | `neg` |
